<vml id="guardrails-for-agent-autonomy" title="Guardrails for Agent Autonomy" fps="24" width="1920" height="1080" poster="81s">
  <voiceover provider="openai" model="gpt-4o-mini-tts" voice="echo" sampleRateHz="24000" leadInSeconds="0.25s" trimEndSeconds="0s" />

  <scene id="guardrails-for-agent-autonomy" title="Guardrails for Agent Autonomy">
    <layer id="background" z="-1">
      <background props='{"color":"#fdfdfd"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="title" z="1">
      <title props='{"text":"Guardrails for Agent Autonomy","x":960,"y":220,"textAlign":"center"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="subtitle" z="0">
      <text-block props='{"text":"Why you cannot drive fast without brakes.","x":960,"y":520,"size":48,"weight":600,"align":"center","maxWidth":1400,"font":"serif"}' />
    </layer>
    <cue id="title" label="title">
      <pause seconds="0.7s" />
      <voice>Guardrails for agent autonomy.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.45s" />
      <voice>Why you can't drive fast without brakes.</voice>
    </cue>
  </scene>

  <transition id="guardrails-push-1" effect="slide" duration="12f" mode="insert" ease="power2.inOut" props='{"direction":"left"}' />

  <scene id="the-paradox-of-power" title="The Paradox of Power">
    <layer id="background" z="-1">
      <background props='{"color":"#fdfdfd"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="title" z="1">
      <title props='{"text":"You cannot drive fast without brakes","x":960,"y":200,"textAlign":"center"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="content" z="0">
      <text-block props='{"text":"If agents can take real actions with side effects, guardrails stop being a nice-to-have. They become the price of admission.\\n\\n• Prompts are suggestions, not controls.\\n• Guardrails are enforceable boundaries.\\n• Start with a threat model: assets, entry points, trust boundaries, and controls.","x":960,"y":610,"size":40,"align":"center","maxWidth":1500,"font":"serif","lineHeight":1.35}' />
    </layer>
    <cue id="brakes" label="brakes">
      <voice>Picture a Formula One car with its brake system removed. Lighter. Simpler. Fewer things to go wrong.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.5s" />
      <voice>You'd crash on the first turn.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.45s" />
      <voice>The best racing teams don't debate whether brakes slow them down. They know something deeper: brakes are what let you go fast in the first place.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.55s" />
      <voice>That's the paradox of agent autonomy. Guardrails are not a limitation on autonomy — they're the prerequisite for it.</voice>
    </cue>
  </scene>

  <transition id="guardrails-push-2" effect="slide" duration="12f" mode="insert" ease="power2.inOut" props='{"direction":"left"}' />

  <scene id="the-pattern-repeats-across-domains" title="The Pattern Repeats Across Domains">
    <layer id="background" z="-1">
      <background props='{"color":"#fdfdfd"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="title" z="1">
      <title props='{"text":"The pattern repeats across domains","x":960,"y":200,"textAlign":"center"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="content" z="0">
      <text-block props='{"text":"Aviation","x":360,"y":420,"size":44,"weight":800,"align":"center","maxWidth":420,"font":"serif"}' />
      <text-block props='{"text":"Hard limits, checklists, and layered safety did not reduce autonomy. They made delegation safe at scale.","x":360,"y":560,"size":34,"align":"center","maxWidth":420,"font":"serif","lineHeight":1.35}' />
      <text-block props='{"text":"Medicine","x":960,"y":420,"size":44,"weight":800,"align":"center","maxWidth":420,"font":"serif"}' />
      <text-block props='{"text":"Protocols and checklists are how experts avoid catastrophic misses under pressure.","x":960,"y":560,"size":34,"align":"center","maxWidth":420,"font":"serif","lineHeight":1.35}' />
      <text-block props='{"text":"Organizations","x":1560,"y":420,"size":44,"weight":800,"align":"center","maxWidth":420,"font":"serif"}' />
      <text-block props='{"text":"Delegation requires boundaries: budgets, approval gates, audits, and reviews. Constraints enable autonomy.","x":1560,"y":560,"size":34,"align":"center","maxWidth":420,"font":"serif","lineHeight":1.35}' />
    </layer>
    <cue id="patterns" label="patterns">
      <voice>This pattern repeats everywhere humans have built powerful, autonomous systems.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.4s" />
      <voice>Aviation scaled autonomy by adding checklists, hard limits, and layered safety. Medicine made protocols standard because expertise alone isn't enough under pressure. Organizations delegate power safely by creating budgets, approvals, audits, and reviews.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.5s" />
      <voice>The more powerful the actor, the more critical the guardrails. AI isn't special — it's just newer.</voice>
    </cue>
  </scene>

  <transition id="guardrails-push-3" effect="slide" duration="12f" mode="insert" ease="power2.inOut" props='{"direction":"left"}' />

  <scene id="the-prompt-engineering-ceiling" title="The Prompt-Engineering Ceiling">
    <layer id="background" z="-1">
      <background props='{"color":"#fdfdfd"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="title" z="1">
      <title props='{"text":"The prompt-engineering ceiling","x":960,"y":180,"textAlign":"center"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="subtitle" z="1">
      <text-block props='{"text":"Prompts can reduce misbehavior - but not with enough reliability to safely scale in production.","x":960,"y":300,"size":32,"align":"center","maxWidth":1500,"font":"serif"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="diagram" z="0">
      <prompt-engineering-ceiling-diagram props='{"containerWidth":1400,"containerHeight":650,"x":960,"y":660}' />
    </layer>
    <cue id="prompt_ceiling" label="prompt_ceiling">
      <voice>Prompts matter. They shape behavior and reduce error rates.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.4s" />
      <voice>But prompts are suggestions, not controls. When an agent has access to powerful tools, you eventually hit a ceiling. You can make failure less likely, but you can't make it vanish.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.5s" />
      <voice>Production safety can't be built out of suggestions alone. You need enforceable boundaries.</voice>
    </cue>
  </scene>

  <transition id="guardrails-push-4" effect="slide" duration="12f" mode="insert" ease="power2.inOut" props='{"direction":"left"}' />

  <scene id="the-manual-assembly-problem" title="The Manual Assembly Problem">
    <layer id="background" z="-1">
      <background props='{"color":"#fdfdfd"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="title" z="1">
      <title props='{"text":"The manual assembly problem","x":960,"y":200,"textAlign":"center"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="content" z="0">
      <text-block props='{"text":"Many teams already add guardrails in Python - schemas, validation, retries, approval gates, sandboxing, secrets hygiene.\\n\\nBut it is easy to miss a layer when you assemble everything by convention across mismatched systems.\\n\\n• Tool schemas and deterministic validation\\n• Policy enforcement (allowlists, limits, invariants)\\n• Approval gates for irreversible actions\\n• Sandboxing and isolation for code and files\\n• Secrets isolation to prevent credential theft","x":960,"y":620,"size":36,"align":"center","maxWidth":1500,"font":"serif","lineHeight":1.35}' />
    </layer>
    <cue id="manual_assembly" label="manual_assembly">
      <voice>The best teams already add guardrails in Python: schemas, validation, retries, approval gates, sandboxing, and secrets hygiene.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.4s" />
      <voice>The problem isn't that people don't know guardrails matter. The problem is that when you assemble everything by convention across mismatched systems, it's easy to miss a layer.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.45s" />
      <voice>Missing a layer won't feel like a mistake until it becomes an incident.</voice>
    </cue>
  </scene>

  <transition id="guardrails-push-5" effect="slide" duration="12f" mode="insert" ease="power2.inOut" props='{"direction":"left"}' />

  <scene id="guardrails-as-first-class-architecture" title="Guardrails as First-Class Architecture">
    <layer id="background" z="-1">
      <background props='{"color":"#fdfdfd"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="title" z="1">
      <title props='{"text":"Guardrails as first-class architecture","x":960,"y":180,"textAlign":"center"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="subtitle" z="1">
      <text-block props='{"text":"No single technique solves everything. Guardrails work as defense in depth - layers that each reduce a different class of risk.","x":960,"y":300,"size":32,"align":"center","maxWidth":1500,"font":"serif"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="diagram" z="0">
      <guardrails-stack-diagram props='{"containerWidth":1600,"containerHeight":650,"x":960,"y":690}' />
    </layer>
    <cue id="defense_in_depth" label="defense_in_depth">
      <voice>This is the philosophy behind Tactus. Guardrails are not add-ons you bolt on later. They're architectural decisions baked into the execution model.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.5s" />
      <voice>No single technique solves everything. Guardrails work as defense in depth: layers that each reduce a different class of risk.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.4s" />
      <voice>At the top: cost and limits. Hard quotas prevent runaway loops before they become billing nightmares.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.35s" />
      <voice>Prompt engineering. Structured instructions guide behavior and reduce error rates.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.35s" />
      <voice>Context engineering. Curated context ensures the model has the right information, not just all information.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.35s" />
      <voice>Model selection. Choose and fine-tune models for specific capabilities and safety profiles.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.35s" />
      <voice>Tool selection. Give the agent only the capabilities it needs, and stage access over time.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.35s" />
      <voice>Code sandboxing. Isolated execution environments prevent unauthorized system access.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.35s" />
      <voice>Container isolation. Ephemeral containers constrain what the runtime can touch and firewall side effects inside the container.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.35s" />
    </cue>
  </scene>

  <transition id="guardrails-push-6" effect="slide" duration="12f" mode="insert" ease="power2.inOut" props='{"direction":"left"}' />

  <scene id="least-privilege-by-design" title="Least Privilege by Design">
    <layer id="background" z="-1">
      <background props='{"color":"#fdfdfd"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="title" z="1">
      <title props='{"text":"Least privilege by design","x":960,"y":180,"textAlign":"center"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="subtitle" z="1">
      <text-block props='{"text":"Tactus enforces least privilege across multiple dimensions - not just tool access, but holistic minimal capability.","x":960,"y":300,"size":32,"align":"center","maxWidth":1500,"font":"serif"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="diagram" z="0">
      <least-privilege-diagram props='{"containerWidth":1600,"containerHeight":650,"x":960,"y":690}' />
    </layer>
    <cue id="least_privilege" label="least_privilege">
      <voice>Tactus enforces least privilege by design, across multiple dimensions.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.4s" />
      <voice>Minimal toolsets: agents get only the tools they need, not a kitchen sink.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.35s" />
      <voice>Curated context: relevant information only, not everything.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.35s" />
      <voice>Network isolation: the runtime is networkless by default.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.35s" />
      <voice>Secretless broker: credentials stay outside, the agent requests work but never holds keys.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.35s" />
      <voice>Temporal gating: tools become available only when the workflow stage requires them.</voice>
    </cue>
  </scene>

  <transition id="guardrails-push-7" effect="slide" duration="12f" mode="insert" ease="power2.inOut" props='{"direction":"left"}' />

  <scene id="sandboxing-a-secretless-broker-boundary" title="Sandboxing + a Secretless Broker Boundary">
    <layer id="background" z="-1">
      <background props='{"color":"#fdfdfd"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="title" z="1">
      <title props='{"text":"Keep the monkey in the box","x":960,"y":180,"textAlign":"center"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="subtitle" z="1">
      <text-block props='{"text":"Sandbox untrusted orchestration. Keep secrets out of the runtime. Broker privileged calls behind a narrow, auditable boundary.","x":960,"y":300,"size":32,"align":"center","maxWidth":1500,"font":"serif"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="diagram" z="0">
      <container-sandbox-diagram props='{"containerWidth":1600,"containerHeight":650,"x":960,"y":690}' />
    </layer>
    <cue id="sandbox_broker" label="sandbox_broker">
      <voice>Once you let an agent write files or run code, you want a cage. Tactus runs orchestration inside a sandboxed Lua environment, and when sandboxing is enabled, inside an ephemeral container.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.5s" />
      <voice>But containers answer only one security question: what can it touch? The other question is: what can it steal?</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.5s" />
      <voice>The broker boundary is the game changer. Keep the runtime secretless and networkless by default. The sandbox can request tool calls, but it never holds provider keys. The keys live outside the sandbox, in a trusted broker.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.45s" />
      <voice>This is the security model: don't make secrets hard to steal—make sure there are no secrets inside the runtime to steal. It's like letting a burglar into an empty building. Even if they get in, there's nothing valuable to take.</voice>
    </cue>
  </scene>

  <transition id="guardrails-push-8" effect="slide" duration="12f" mode="insert" ease="power2.inOut" props='{"direction":"left"}' />

  <scene id="a-concrete-example" title="A Concrete Example">
    <layer id="background" z="-1">
      <background props='{"color":"#fdfdfd"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="title" z="1">
      <title props='{"text":"A concrete example: recap emails","x":960,"y":200,"textAlign":"center"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="content" z="0">
      <text-block props='{"text":"A safe delegation pattern\\n\\n1) Draft with read-only tools (no side effects).\\n2) Durable human review: approve, edit, reject.\\n3) Only after approval does the send tool become available.","x":960,"y":600,"size":40,"align":"center","maxWidth":1400,"font":"serif","lineHeight":1.35}' />
    </layer>
    <cue id="recap_emails" label="recap_emails">
      <voice>Consider a workflow that drafts and sends recap emails from meeting notes.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.4s" />
      <voice>Without guardrails, you either supervise every run, or you give the agent side-effect tools and accept unacceptable risk.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.45s" />
      <voice>With staged tools and durable approvals, the agent drafts with read-only tools, a human reviews at a checkpoint, and only after approval does the send tool become available.</voice>
    </cue>
  </scene>

  <transition id="guardrails-push-9" effect="slide" duration="12f" mode="insert" ease="power2.inOut" props='{"direction":"left"}' />

  <scene id="closing" title="Closing">
    <layer id="background" z="-1">
      <background props='{"color":"#fdfdfd"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="title" z="1">
      <title props='{"text":"Guardrails are the engine of delegation","x":960,"y":240,"textAlign":"center"}' />
    </layer>
    <layer id="content" z="0">
      <text-block props='{"text":"The race car needs brakes. The surgeon needs protocols. The organization needs governance. The agent needs guardrails.\\n\\nRead the full story at tactus dot run slash guardrails.","x":960,"y":600,"size":36,"align":"center","maxWidth":1500,"font":"serif","lineHeight":1.35}' />
    </layer>
    <cue id="closing" label="closing">
      <voice>Guardrails aren't a tax. They're the engine of delegation.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.4s" />
      <voice>The race car needs brakes. The surgeon needs protocols. The organization needs governance. The agent needs guardrails.</voice>
      <pause seconds="0.5s" />
      <voice>Read the full story at tactus dot run slash guardrails.</voice>
    </cue>
  </scene>
</vml>
